# Build context exclusions for the repo root.
#
# Docker only reads `.dockerignore` from the root of the build context, so
# docker/.dockerignore has never applied to any build — every image is built
# with a context of `.` or `services/<name>`, never `docker/`.
#
# Without this file a root-context build uploads node_modules (~2.9k packages)
# and every .next/dist directory to the daemon before the first instruction
# runs.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image from package-lock.json
**/node_modules

# Build output — rebuilt inside the image
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Python
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# VCS and CI
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local environment — never bake secrets into an image
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Test, scan and coverage artifacts
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/coverage-report.json
trivy-results*.sarif

# Avatar Studio reconstruction artifacts (AVATAR_STORAGE_DIR)
var/

# Editor and OS noise
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
